WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.720
That viral exosome serum?

2
00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.100
The word “exosome”

3
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.360
tells you almost nothing.

4
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.700
Exosomes are microscopic particles

5
00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.500
cells release to carry signals.

6
00:00:08.976 --> 00:00:11.630
But in skincare, they can come
from very different sources.

7
00:00:12.029 --> 00:00:14.700
And those sources are not
automatically interchangeable.

8
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.700
The research is promising,

9
00:00:16.885 --> 00:00:17.990
but human evidence

10
00:00:18.091 --> 00:00:20.700
for topical exosome skincare
is still limited.

11
00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:25.100
Many studies also combine exosomes
with procedures like microneedling,

12
00:00:25.496 --> 00:00:27.880
making it difficult to credit
the serum alone.

13
00:00:28.489 --> 00:00:29.900
So before you buy one,

14
00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:31.700
ask three questions.

15
00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:33.250
What is the source?

16
00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:35.500
Has the ingredient been
properly characterized,

17
00:00:35.745 --> 00:00:36.900
and kept stable?

18
00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.000
And was this exact
finished product

19
00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:40.560
tested on people?

20
00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:43.300
If the brand only says
“exosome technology,”

21
00:00:44.153 --> 00:00:45.900
that is a marketing claim.

22
00:00:46.388 --> 00:00:48.100
Not proof of a miracle.

23
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:49.850
Promising? Yes.

24
00:00:50.078 --> 00:00:51.650
Proven miracle?

25
00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.100
Not yet.

26
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.300
Comment the exact product,

27
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.560
and SeoulHabit will decode
its label next.
